   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "I would like to obtain the syntax to identify the common method biais CMB  in a model using Unmeasured Latent Method Construct (ULMC). Does someone know this syntax ?<div>Thanks for your responses.</div><div><br></div><div>Richard</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "dmGhhRsnBwAJ",
   "from": "Rönkkö, Mikko",
   "author": "bfa43814f6ba1969",
   "date": "2024-11-08T06:43:58Z",
   "subject": "Re: R CFA lavaan and Common Method Bias (syntax)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Here is an example:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">library(lavaan); library(MASS); set.seed(22)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Lambda &lt;- cbind(rep(1,12), diag(3)[rep(1:3,each=4),])<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">rownames(Lambda) &lt;- paste(&quot;x&quot;,1:12,sep=&quot;&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"FI\" style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">Sigma &lt;- Lambda %*% t(Lambda) + diag(12)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">data &lt;- mvrnorm(100,rep(0,12),Sigma)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">#cfa(&quot;M1 =~ x1 + x2 + x3 + x4<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">#     M2 =~ x5 + x6 + x7 + x8<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">#     G =~ x1 + x2 + x3 + x4 + x5 + x6 + x7 + x8&quot;, data)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">cfa(&quot;M1 =~ x1 + x2 + x3 + x4<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">     M2 =~ x5 + x6 + x7 + x8<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">     M3 =~ x9 + x10 + x11 + x12<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">     G =~ x1 + x2 + x3 + x4 + x5 + x6 + x7 + x8 + x9 + x10 + x11 + x12&quot;, data)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\">The example also shows why we should not trust these models: they are often empirically underidentified. The example comes from my lecture on identification of these models. You can find the code in the notes\r\n of slide 25.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><a href=\"https://youtu.be/PFyO2F98eYQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://youtu.be/PFyO2F98eYQ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792414129486000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2rzRaQquEsuNAn-HLor6BT\">https://youtu.be/PFyO2F98eYQ</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><a href=\"https://osf.io/tjxva\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://osf.io/tjxva&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792414129486000&amp;usg=AOvVaw35naLgZc69VGuhgFdpouJd\">https://osf.io/tjxva</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;color:black\">Best regards,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;color:black\">Mikko </span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
